      {
        "label": "SCI",
        "title": "Recognised as an international standard (ISO/IEC 21031:2024)",
        "bodyHtml": "SCI went from first draft in December 2021 to an ISO standard in March 2024, in under three years. ISO standards for software typically take five to seven. <a href='https://greensoftware.foundation/articles/sci-specification-achieves-iso-standard-status/'>Read the announcement</a>.",
        "tags": [
          "sci"
        ],
        "ctaText": "View source",
        "ctaHref": "https://www.iso.org/standard/86612.html",
        "secondaryCtaText": "Learn more about SCI",
        "secondaryCtaHref": "/standards/sci/"
      },
      {
        "label": "SCI for AI",
        "title": "A way to measure the carbon impact of AI",
        "bodyHtml": "SCI for AI extends ISO/IEC 21031 to AI systems, giving organisations a consistent method for calculating the carbon impact of the AI they build or use. It was ratified in December 2025 after 11 months of work with more than 20 partner organisations. <a href='https://greensoftware.foundation/stories/sci-for-ai/'>How it was built</a>, with contributors from Siemens, IMDA Singapore, Google, Microsoft and UBS.",
        "tags": [
          "sci-ai"
        ],
        "ctaText": "View source",
        "ctaHref": "https://sci-for-ai.greensoftware.foundation/",
        "secondaryCtaText": "Learn more about SCI for AI",
        "secondaryCtaHref": "/standards/sci-ai/"
      },
      {
        "label": "Real Time Cloud",
        "title": "Built with Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud and AWS",
        "bodyHtml": "Ratified in April 2025, Real Time Cloud lets cloud providers share live energy and carbon data in a common format. A working group including Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud and AWS built it.",
        "tags": [
          "rtc"
        ],
        "ctaText": "View source",
        "ctaHref": "https://greensoftware.foundation/stories/real-time-cloud/",
        "secondaryCtaText": "Learn more about Real Time Cloud",
        "secondaryCtaHref": "/standards/rtc/"
      },
      {
        "label": "W3C",
        "title": "A formal partnership with the body that sets web standards",
        "bodyHtml": "GSF runs SCI for Web through its consensus process while the W3C's Sustainable Web group gives feedback.",
        "tags": [
          "sci-web"
        ],
        "ctaText": "View source",
        "ctaHref": "https://greensoftware.foundation/articles/the-green-software-foundation-and-world-wide-web-consortium-w3c-collaborate-to-ad/",
        "secondaryCtaText": "Learn more about SCI for Web",
        "secondaryCtaHref": "/standards/sci-web/"
      },
      {
        "label": "SCI",
        "title": "SCI in practice and in research",
        "bodyHtml": "At least seven independent organisations have published results using SCI, and more than 15 peer-reviewed papers since 2022, including at the ACM conferences on fairness, accountability and transparency (FAccT) and on cloud computing (SoCC), refer to it. Selected examples are listed under Member case studies and Research.",
        "tags": [
          "sci"
        ],
        "ctaText": "View source",
        "ctaHref": "https://greensoftware.foundation/standards/sci/",
        "secondaryCtaText": "See the research papers",
        "secondaryCtaHref": "#research"
      },
      {
        "label": "SCI for AI Bootcamp",
